.TH CLAUDE\-HELPER 1 "" "claude-helper" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claude\-helper, ch \- Several Claude Code accounts, one configuration, and the tools around it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBclaude\-helper\fR \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR...]
.br
\fBclaude\fR [\fIclaude arguments\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Several Claude Code accounts on one Linux machine, with one configuration and one session
database, plus the small tools that make living with many sessions bearable.
.PP
The same entry point answers under several names:
.TP
.B claude
Claude Code on the current profile. bin/ must come last in PATH, so this wrapper wins over
the binary of the official installer.
.TP
.B claude\-browser
the $BROWSER of the sessions: opens a URL in the browser window of the account.
.TP
.BR claude\-helper ", " ch
everything else, described below.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS profile
accounts: list, use, switch, init…
.PP
\fBclaude\-helper profile list [\-\-offline]\fR
.RS
profiles, account, organization, quota (5 h / 7 days); * = current
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
do not call the API for the quota
.RE
.PP
\fBclaude\-helper profile current\fR
.RS
print the current profile
.RE
.PP
\fBclaude\-helper profile use name\fR
.RS
set the current profile: the one `claude` launches
.RE
.PP
\fBclaude\-helper profile switch [\-\-force] name\fR
.RS
use + relaunch every open session on that profile (\-\-resume)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
do not wait for a session to be idle
.RE
.PP
\fBclaude\-helper profile live\fR
.RS
open sessions: pid, profile, status, how they can be relaunched
.RE
.PP
\fBclaude\-helper profile init name\fR
.RS
create ~/.claude\-<name> and link it to the main profile
.RE
.PP
\fBclaude\-helper profile sync [name]\fR
.RS
lay the links again, reconcile the MCP servers
.TP
\fIname\fR
default: every profile
.RE
.PP
\fBclaude\-helper profile run <name> [claude arguments…]\fR
.RS
sync, launch Claude on <name> with the remaining arguments, sync again
.RE
.PP
\fBclaude\-helper profile doctor [name]\fR
.RS
check the setup without changing anything
.RE
.SS sessions
find past conversations: latest, by word typed, by name
.PP
\fBclaude\-helper sessions [\-\-name WORD] [\-\-here] [\-n N] [word]\fR
.TP
\fIword\fR
a word you typed in the conversation
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fIWORD\fR
match the session name (/rename) or its project folder
.TP
\fB\-\-here\fR
only the project of the current directory
.TP
\fB\-n\fR \fIN\fR
how many (default 15)
.SS recall
wake a session up, even closed: it answers, then exits
.PP
\fBclaude\-helper recall [\-\-write] target question\fR
.TP
\fItarget\fR
session name (/rename) or id
.TP
\fB\-\-write\fR
move the real conversation forward instead of a fork
.SS md
browse the CLAUDE.md files, or show what a directory loads
.PP
\fBclaude\-helper md [\-\-junk] [directory]\fR
.TP
\fIdirectory\fR
show the cascade a session opened there loads
.TP
\fB\-\-junk\fR
frozen copies and broken links
.SS browser
open URLs in the browser window of a profile's account
.PP
\fBclaude\-helper browser [\-\-profile PROFILE] [\-\-list] [\-\-dry\-run] [urls ...]\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR, \fB\-p\fR \fIPROFILE\fR
default: the profile of this process, else the current one
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
windows already created
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR, \fB\-n\fR
print the command, open nothing
.SH PROFILES
A profile is a CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR. The main profile is ~/.claude itself; every other profile
is ~/.claude\-<name>, with its own login, token and account, and everything else (CLAUDE.md,
settings, skills, plugins, projects/ with the transcripts and memory) a symlink to the main
profile.
.PP
A /login inside a session does not move the claude.ai MCP servers to the new account: they
stay bound to the account the process started with. That is why
.B profile switch
stops every open session once idle and resumes it with \-\-resume on the new profile.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/claude\-helper/config.toml
settings, every key optional: main_profile, claude_bin, md_roots, browser.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/claude\-helper/
current profile, relaunch markers, switch.log (resume commands of the sessions that could
not be relaunched).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/claude\-helper/browser/
one browser profile per account.
.TP
.I <config>/sessions/<pid>.json
Claude Code's own registry of open sessions, read by switch and live.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLAUDE_PROFILE
the profile of this process; a session never changes account under its own feet.
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
Claude Code's configuration directory, set by the wrapper from the profile.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBclaude\-helper\fR \fIcommand\fR \fB\-\-help\fR,
the README: https://github.com/AlexisLaporte/claude\-helper
